panels.description:
Share of placed pods by who chose the node: the score plugin or extender whose weighted score gave the chosen node the largest part of its lead over the runner-up (the best other node that passed the filters). A plugin with a large share drives placement; a plugin that never appears does not change placements in practice. Legend values:

- `plugin/<name>`: a score plugin of kube-scheduler, e.g. `plugin/NodeResourcesFit`, `plugin/TaintToleration`.
- `extender/<name>`: a scheduler extender, named after its KubeSchedulerWebhookConfiguration, e.g. `extender/usage-extender`. An extender configured without one is named by its URL.
- `scheduler/<case>`: kube-scheduler itself decided, scoring did not pick the node:
  - `scheduler/single-node`: only one node passed the filters, there was no choice;
  - `scheduler/tie`: the best nodes had equal total scores, the winner was picked at random;
  - `scheduler/nominated-node`: the pod took the node nominated for it during preemption;
  - `scheduler/node-hint`: (Kubernetes 1.35+) the scheduler took the node from the batching hint without scoring.

With percentageOfNodesToScore below 100 the runner-up and ties are relative to the scored subset of nodes. Simulations and pods placed by the pod group cycle (Kubernetes 1.36+) are not counted.

